WEBVTT

00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:06.880
The Second Wave, a disaster that was sure to come...

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:13.300
...brought humanity's hearts together over the span of two centuries.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.850
With the Great Mission over, now is the time...

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:21.020
...that people are turning their eyes outside the Sol System.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:28.850
But that was the start of people gazing at the future with various views.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars, Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて 飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Carry the unexpierence of the heart in the hands and go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて go far away

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
Urayamu koto ni Narete shimattara

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
If you have experienced the envy

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
羨む事に 慣れてしまったら

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Hokoreru jibun ga Toozakatteku

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Your proud self will go far away

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
誇れる自分が 遠ざかってく

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Mienai tsubasa de habataku no fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Flapping the invisible wings to fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
見えない翼で羽ばたくの fly higher

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
Yume wo egaku no wa hito ni umareta kara

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
I'm imaging dreams because I was born a "person"

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
夢を描くのは「人」に生まれたから

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Carry the unexperienced of the heart in the hands

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
Anata to nara Yowai jibun wo sarakedashite hashiridaseru no

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
If I were with you, I'd start running, exposing my weak self

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
あなたとなら 弱い自分をさらけ出して走り出せるの

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
Mirai yo dou ka Mugen ni tsuzuke go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
The future! Somehow continues to the infinity, go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
未来よどうか 無限に続け go far away

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:04.010
Episode Eleven:
 The Real You

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:04.060
Man...

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:06.770
It was prettier when it was green.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:08.270
Outer space?

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:11.540
Yeah, somehow red seems kind of sad.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:13.680
I wonder what the reason is?

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:16.770
Since I'm below you two, all I'm concerned about are the final tests.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:20.150
Whether it's green or red, I'll leave that to you to think about, Milady.

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:24.000
Outer space, set ablaze by our passion...

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:27.380
Yes, that is... our passionate hearts.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:28.400
Huh?

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:29.150
Hmm?
Huh?

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:32.790
So who are you trying to hit on?

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:35.730
Oh my, you're shaking!

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:37.010
W-W-Who is?!

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:39.730
You're so obvious!

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.900
What? Who is? Who was he hitting on?

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:42.910
S-Shut up!

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:45.830
You, and you, shut up!

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:47.620
Your cheeks are red!
He's turning red!

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:49.280
I wonder what color it is.

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:50.000
Huh?

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:54.850
I want to see outer space beyond this...

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:00.010
So the preparatory students...

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:02.290
...are finally going to see their own outer space, are they?

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:03.210
Yes...

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:07.790
Well, this will be harder for them than their first flight.

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:10.900
The D.L.S. Isn't based on reason, after all.

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:15.620
In any case, I don't want them to be rash.

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:19.950
Although that's why we're there to support them...

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:26.660
But this year's preparatory students might be better than we expect...

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:27.270
What?

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:36.290
Well, they were able to handle that thing out of the blue, so...

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:38.140
Let's go.

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:41.210
We can't set an example as the assistants if we're late.

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:46.180
When you master the D.L.S...

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:50.000
...you'll be able to feel outer space more closely.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:51.990
Today will be your first step towards that.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:55.150
I believe that you already know quite well...

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:56.590
...the difference between a simulation and actual practice.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.410
All units, try and fly at your own pace.

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:04.140
Two members from the Big Four will keep an eye on you.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:07.810
It's all right if you damage the Biancas a little.

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:09.200
After this...

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.660
...all units will get a complete system check and undergo maintenance.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:13.520
All right, begin!

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:29.530
I don't understand any of this!

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:38.840
I feel like throwing up...

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:51.940
Wow!

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:55.150
This feels awful! This is fun!

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:07.810
Um... there! No, not that...

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:18.400
Turn off your system!

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:20.260
Let inertia take over!
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:26.060
The D.L.S. Lets you visualize all kinds of information.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:29.510
The invisible becomes visible.

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:31.470
You have to feel the information.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:47.690
The Big Four are impressive, as always.

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:49.400
That's a splendid show of skill.

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.360
When you master the D.L.S...

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:54.540
...your machine truly becomes like a part of your body.

00:05:57.550 --> 00:05:58.700
Next, Katase!

00:05:59.020 --> 00:05:59.490
Yes, ma'am!

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:16.610
What?

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:17.620
What is this?

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:21.670
This sensation... it's similar...

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:23.660
Release all gravity generators now.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:25.170
Time to do this, Shima-chan.

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:27.130
Otoyama...

00:06:27.710 --> 00:06:30.050
Oh, no, what am I thinking about?

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:31.350
Katase, is anything wrong?

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:33.410
No, nothing at all!

00:06:44.510 --> 00:06:47.910
You'll be all right. It's like getting motion sickness.

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:52.350
Just as it says, the D.L.S. Is a system that directly links to you.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:53.390
Okay...

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:58.420
Anyone with compressed information relayed directly into their brain...

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:00.620
...via their optic nerves would feel bad.

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:02.900
You'll get used to it soon.

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:26.030
I'm going to the B3 classroom next.

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:27.570
Okay, see you later.

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:28.150
Right.

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:29.500
Oh...

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:32.770
Thank you very much for earlier.

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:34.280
You're welcome.

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:42.600
She was magnificent.

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:43.330
What?

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:45.070
Miss Katase.

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:47.440
Did you give her any advice?

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:49.280
No.

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:50.610
I see...

00:07:56.690 --> 00:07:58.920
Well, this is impressive.

00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:00.070
What is?

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:01.170
Katase.

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:05.130
On her first D.L.S. Trial, out of the blue, she's in the top ten.

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:06.000
Oh.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:08.950
This means the regular students can't let their guard down.

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:11.060
Once they're using the same system...

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:12.560
...it doesn't matter if they're preparatory students or not.

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:15.110
But the Katies are superior in terms of machine performance.

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:18.840
If they lose to a Bianca, it would be a disgrace to the regular students.

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:21.290
Kouta Otoyama...

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:23.950
He's at rank C again, is he?

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:29.450
Man, I still feel spaced out...

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:31.330
Oh, how pathetic.

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:34.050
If you give up after that, what's to become of you?

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:36.680
Just because you happen to be suited for this...

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:40.360
All I can hear are the complaints of a loser.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:43.360
Are you all right?

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:44.750
Yeah...

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:48.800
Is there a trick to it?

00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:49.490
What?

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:51.540
The D.L.S.

00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:55.530
If there is one, tell me, would you?

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:04.030
Rinna.

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:06.120
Here you are.

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:07.620
Shipon...

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:09.590
Thank you.

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:10.340
Sure.

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:17.030
Rinna, you're going home soon, right?

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:17.570
Yeah...

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:21.350
Well, the Second Wave has already gone by.

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:24.680
Even if you go back to the Ultima, there's no school there, right?

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.540
So why not use this as a chance to actually transfer here?

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:34.160
I wonder if the Third Wave or something will come.

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:37.520
Since Shipon's here, she could take it out with Infi.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:43.160
Just the rest of this month, huh?

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:53.600
Yo.

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:54.520
Heya.

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:57.380
You by yourself?

00:09:57.740 --> 00:09:59.030
You can tell by looking at me, right?

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:00.770
Well, true enough.

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:05.130
Hey...
If it's a joke, then I've had enough.

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:07.530
That's not it.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:08.980
The D.L.S...

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:12.940
When you're using it, it's better to not use your head.

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:15.690
Give the sensations over to your body.

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:18.250
That's what Kouta said.

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:23.790
Everyone's so amazing.

00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:26.130
Shipon is, and so is Milady...

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:29.340
We all started out the same...

00:10:29.890 --> 00:10:31.970
...but it feels like they've gotten a pretty big lead on me.

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:37.090
Doesn't your neck get tired from looking up all the time?

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:40.850
I think it would be a little more comfortable if you looked forward...

00:10:41.650 --> 00:10:42.520
Just kidding!

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:47.470
Well, yeah, I do say good things!

00:10:47.730 --> 00:10:49.830
This doesn't happen often, so be grateful.

00:11:05.110 --> 00:11:06.340
She was magnificent.

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:10.250
Did you give her any advice?

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:48.740
Good morning! It's unusual to see you by yourself.

00:11:48.990 --> 00:11:50.940
Yeah. Arisa went to the co-op.

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:52.820
I saw the bulletin board.

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:55.860
You're in the top ten of the whole preparatory student class.

00:11:58.530 --> 00:11:59.820
Somehow, it's similar.

00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:01.290
Huh? To what?

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:04.360
To the sensation when you and Infi were in motion.

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:05.510
That might be it.

00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:06.670
Oh...?

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:09.620
But why, Otoyama?
What?

00:12:10.170 --> 00:12:13.230
You should be able to control it much better than me, but...

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:16.470
Hmm... Yeah, I wonder why.

00:12:16.720 --> 00:12:18.820
Otoyama, you really do go at your own pace.

00:12:19.390 --> 00:12:20.780
Yesterday, I was trying as hard as I could.

00:12:21.270 --> 00:12:22.690
I did the same when we were in Infi.

00:12:23.330 --> 00:12:24.660
I don't understand it, either.

00:12:25.150 --> 00:12:27.000
Oh, I see.

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:31.020
Just thinking about it is useless, so I don't think about it.

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:32.380
What's with that?

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:39.330
Bread fresh from the oven is the best!

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:40.740
So that girl was her?

00:12:40.810 --> 00:12:42.470
Yeah, Shima Katase.

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:44.750
What's with her? She's completely normal.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:46.000
She's seems slow.

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:59.410
There's talk of Shima Katase skipping grades.

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:01.720
It's not... improbable.

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:02.760
No.

00:13:03.150 --> 00:13:06.620
It's no joke. She might really be a genius.

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:07.950
That's true.

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:15.610
No preparatory student's skipped grades since Ayaka.

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:20.060
Geniuses do exist.

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:24.230
I bet she doesn't have to work at all and can do anything.

00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:27.720
I'm jealous. I wish I had been born a genius.

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:29.520
Then you could have as much fun as you wanted.

00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:30.760
A rose-colored life.

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:36.200
Be conscious of your own imperfections...

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:38.770
...before you talk about other people's.

00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:42.990
There's no such thing as geniuses in this world.

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:51.440
The you that came to the Stellvia...

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:53.860
What were you seeking?

00:13:54.470 --> 00:13:55.690
What were you aiming for?

00:13:58.260 --> 00:14:00.830
Where is the real you right now?

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:14.890
What? No way!

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:16.860
You're exaggerating.
Really.

00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:20.700
But getting called on by one of the Big Four is incredible.

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:23.360
Well, I think that's true.

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:24.490
Miss Katase?

00:14:24.950 --> 00:14:28.140
If you would be all right with it, would you join the Big Four?

00:14:28.480 --> 00:14:30.700
What would you do if that's what they want to talk about?

00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:33.220
Miss Machida isn't like that!

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:35.150
It's all right.
No, it's not!

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:37.350
So what does she want to talk about?

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:38.830
I don't know.

00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:42.320
We just spoke for a moment in the hallway a little while ago.

00:14:42.470 --> 00:14:45.050
She asked if I'd talk to her for a little bit after school.

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:46.760
You may have been chosen as a candidate to succeed them...

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:47.510
Are the Big Four like that? You may have been chosen as a candidate to succeed them...

00:14:47.730 --> 00:14:49.040
Are the Big Four like that? ...because you're amazing, Shipon.

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:52.650
Aren't they the Big Four because they're four amazing people? 

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:53.460
In any case, be sure to report every last aspect of your discussion.

00:14:53.840 --> 00:14:54.970
Understand?

00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:57.660
Snap! Roger!

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:00.000
Shipon...

00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:00.600
Huh?

00:15:01.760 --> 00:15:02.600
What's wrong?

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.850
Er, no, never mind.

00:15:05.230 --> 00:15:06.190
You're acting strange.

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:09.740
I'm looking forward to it.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:14.090
But what'll I do if I'm so nervous I can't speak?

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:15.500
Cover it up by laughing.

00:15:15.730 --> 00:15:20.010
But then she'll think I'm a bubble-head, and get mad at me.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:33.440
What do you see?

00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:35.510
I was spaced out.

00:15:36.980 --> 00:15:37.950
I see.

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:43.230
Well, you see, I have a slight interest in what you see.

00:15:52.310 --> 00:15:53.840
There's no need to be nervous.

00:15:54.420 --> 00:15:56.530
Oh, r-right... I'm sorry.

00:15:56.760 --> 00:16:01.100
No need to apologize, either. I'm a normal student, just like you.

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:02.330
What?

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:03.500
No, you're not.

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:05.490
You're an amazing person, Miss Machida!

00:16:05.550 --> 00:16:06.940
Everyone looks up to you!

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:10.260
You're smart, good at flying, and a real beauty!

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:12.490
I'm just a kid...

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:16.380
O-Oh no, why am I getting so worked up?

00:16:28.510 --> 00:16:31.060
Miss Katase, why did you come up into space?

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:34.180
I wanted to see the stars normally.

00:16:34.350 --> 00:16:35.080
Normally?

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:36.780
Yes.

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:40.540
Not look up at them, but like this.

00:16:42.510 --> 00:16:45.140
So perhaps there was no special need to be a pilot, then?

00:16:45.680 --> 00:16:48.060
Oh... perhaps not.

00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:51.120
I see.
But!

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:53.920
But now, I want to get even better.

00:16:54.190 --> 00:16:55.360
Better and better!

00:16:55.900 --> 00:16:57.800
Even I thought it was outrageous...

00:16:58.030 --> 00:17:01.620
...to even think of aiming for the Space Academy.

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:04.110
But I'm glad I came.

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:06.830
I'm really glad I came.

00:17:10.980 --> 00:17:13.040
Every day is really fun.

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:21.630
Miss Katase, space isn't a place where you have fun.

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:25.040
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes!

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:26.990
Oh!

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:28.170
Where's Shipon?

00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:29.760
Not here yet.

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:31.690
She called before and said she was having...

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:33.660
...a little independent training with Miss Machida.

00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:39.590
Milady?

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:42.020
It might be...

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:57.600
Every unit will get a complete system check and undergo maintenance.

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:00.380
It can't be...

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:02.840
What's wrong?

00:18:03.620 --> 00:18:05.650
Please! Go to where Shipon is!

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:07.700
She'll be destroyed by Machida!

00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:09.000
By Ayaka Machida!

00:18:09.550 --> 00:18:11.080
That's the kind of person she is!

00:18:19.380 --> 00:18:20.100
Are you ready?

00:18:20.980 --> 00:18:22.360
Yes, I'm ready!

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:52.460
Incredible...

00:18:53.280 --> 00:18:55.440
She hit me twice in that one instant...

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:10.620
I wanted to see the stars normally.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:13.710
I want to look at my own potential.

00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:26.670
I can still do this!

00:19:27.780 --> 00:19:28.950
Ayaka...

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:45.260
Stop it. Shipon is...

00:19:46.010 --> 00:19:46.790
Please...

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:00.090
Trouble? An emergency stop?

00:20:07.380 --> 00:20:08.360
I want to get better.

00:20:08.830 --> 00:20:10.250
I want to improve myself.

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:25.130
This is low of you, Miss Machida!

00:20:54.570 --> 00:20:55.850
Otoyama?

00:21:22.930 --> 00:21:26.090
Have you seen his flight records?

00:21:26.960 --> 00:21:29.590
Those are not the movements of a Bianca.

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:34.630
Kouta Otoyama is the chosen one of the universe.

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:38.870
There might come a time when we'll need him to board that again.

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:42.290
Word has come from the Ultima.

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:46.830
The flying objects from before seem to be appearing frequently.

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
kono sora no iku hate ni

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
<i>Where the end of this sky goes</i>

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
<i>この空の行く果てに</i>

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
mada mienu mirai no nami ga ri

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
<i>Are waves of the future that cannot yet be seen</i>

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
<i>まだ見えぬ 未来の波があり</i>

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
ikite iru ikutsu mono unmei o koete yuku

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
<i>We are alive; we overcome many destinies</i>

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
<i>生きている いくつもの運命を越えて行く</i>

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
dare ni osowari dare ni koute iru no darou

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
<i>Who are we learning from, who are we asking?</i>

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
<i>誰に教わり 誰に請うているのだろう</i>

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
hito wa tsukiru inochi no aima ni

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
<i>People do not have time to fear encountering</i>

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
<i>人は尽きる命の合間に</i>

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
deau koto ni obieru ma wa nai

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
<i>The space between expiring lives</i>

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
<i>出会うことに 怯える間はない</i>

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
tatoe kyou de kono sekai ga owarou to shite ite mo

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
<i>Even if this world would end today</i>

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
<i>たとえ今日で この世界が終わろうとしていても</i>

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
kimi o ai suru darou

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
<i>I will still love you</i>

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
<i>君を愛するだろう</i>

00:23:05.020 --> 00:23:07.030
Next Episode

00:23:06.460 --> 00:23:07.470
This is Rinna!

00:23:07.500 --> 00:23:08.170
This is Yayoi!

00:23:08.280 --> 00:23:10.080
I wonder if Shipon is all right.

00:23:10.220 --> 00:23:12.600
Her Bianca got damaged, but she's all right.

00:23:12.670 --> 00:23:15.340
Why? Why did Ayaka do something like that?

00:23:16.270 --> 00:23:19.310
Well, maybe because she's Ayaka Machida.

00:23:19.380 --> 00:23:22.740
That's weird. Hey, hey, more importantly, it's my farewell party!

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:23.350
That's right!

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:25.750
We're combining it with Christmas, so let's have a splendid party!

00:23:25.890 --> 00:23:29.080
Akira seems kind of down, too. Let's really have a blast!

00:23:29.470 --> 00:23:32.040
On the next episode of Stellvia of the Universe, "Confession"

00:23:32.050 --> 00:23:35.060
Episode 12 
Confession

00:23:32.120 --> 00:23:32.910
Please look forward to it!

00:23:33.090 --> 00:23:34.270
See you later!
